From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 07:28:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: amlogic: vdec: add the module device table

Without the OF device table in the module, udev cannot load the module
for the decoder node, and the decoder stays unbound.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/amlogic/vdec/aml_vdec_drv.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/vdec/aml_vdec_drv.c b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/vdec/aml_vdec_drv.c
index 55668d01b526..6afe482141a8 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/vdec/aml_vdec_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/vdec/aml_vdec_drv.c
@@ -223,6 +223,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id aml_vdec_match[] = {
 	{.compatible = "amlogic,s4-vcodec-dec", .data = &aml_vdec_s4_pdata},
 	{},
 };
+MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, aml_vdec_match);
 
 static struct platform_driver aml_vcodec_dec_driver = {
 	.probe    = aml_vdec_drv_probe,
